% Osteogenesis Stimulators: LCD L33796 and its Policy Article A52513 (DME
% MACs). A policy program of the DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le
% (orders, delivery, benefit category, continued need, refills) and states
% when a claim for a non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator (E0747),
% a spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator (E0748), an ultrasonic
% osteogenesis stimulator (E0760) or the ultrasound conductive coupling gel
% (A4559) is REASONABLE AND NECESSARY. The invasive stimulator (E0749) is
% within the policy's scope but in no benefit of this model: "The DME MAC
% does not process claims for an invasive osteogenesis stimulator"; a
% disposable device, billed A9270, is not decided here.
%
% The criteria. E0747 for any of: a nonunion of a long bone fracture (a
% clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal or
% metatarsal) documented by two sets of radiographs before treatment,
% separated by at least 90 days, each with multiple views and a written
% interpretation stating no clinically significant evidence of healing
% between them; a failed fusion of a joint other than in the spine at least
% nine months after the last surgery; congenital pseudarthrosis. E0748 for
% any of: a failed spinal fusion at least nine months after the last
% surgery; following a multilevel spinal fusion (three or more vertebrae);
% following a spinal fusion with a history of a previously failed fusion at
% the same site. E0760 for all of: a nonunion documented by the same two
% sets of radiographs; a fracture not of the skull or vertebrae; not tumor
% related; and not used with other noninvasive stimulators — a fresh
% fracture or a delayed union, not being a nonunion, has no rule. A4559 when
% the ultrasonic stimulator is covered.
%
% How the criteria are read. Dates and numbers are the record's: the dates
% of the two radiograph sets and of the start of treatment (the LCD's
% "radiographic evidence that fracture healing has ceased for three or more
% months prior to starting treatment" is the first set at least 90 days
% before the second and the second before treatment), the date of the last
% fusion surgery, the number of vertebrae fused. Nine months is read as 274
% days and 90 days as 90. What the record states as fact — the bone, the
% multiple views of each set, the failed fusion, the surgery and its levels,
% the tumor, the concurrent stimulator, congenital pseudarthrosis (the
% shared template "the medical record of B documents C") — is a scenario
% fact. One criterion is a clinical judgment, the judged template of
% dmepos.le "the finding F about B is established" (or unsupported), with
% who found it and why:
%   fracture healing ceased (the treating practitioner's written
%   interpretation of the two sets of radiographs stating that there has
%   been no clinically significant evidence of fracture healing between
%   them — accepted or rejected by the reviewer who reads the films).
% E0747, E0748 and E0760 are on the CMS required face-to-face encounter and
% written order prior to delivery list that dmepos.le reads. The article's
% certificate of medical necessity (CMS Form 847) for dates of service
% before 1 January 2023 and the KF/KX/GA/GZ modifiers are not modelled: the
% policy declares no documentation requirements of its own.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    *a beneficiary* has a fracture of *a bone*; undefined.
    the radiographs of the fracture of *a beneficiary* obtained on *a date* include multiple views of the fracture site; undefined.
    osteogenesis stimulator treatment of *a beneficiary* started on *a date*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has a failed fusion of *a joint*; undefined.
    the last fusion surgery of *a beneficiary* was on *a date*; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* had spinal fusion surgery on *a date* involving *a number* vertebrae; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* has a history of a previously failed spinal fusion at the same site; undefined.
    the fracture of *a beneficiary* is tumor related; undefined.
    *an item* is used concurrently with other noninvasive osteogenesis stimulators; undefined.
    % the knowledge base
    *a bone* is a long bone.
    % derived
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for a spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator.
    *a beneficiary* meets the criteria for an ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator.
    the nonunion of the fracture of *a beneficiary* is documented by radiographs before treatment.
    *an item* is a covered ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator.

the knowledge base osteogenesis stimulators includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base osteogenesis stimulators includes:

LCD L33796 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33796".
the text of LCD L33796 is at "sources/lcd/L33796.txt".
Policy Article A52513 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52513".
the text of Policy Article A52513 is at "sources/article/A52513.txt".

% The long bones (the LCD's appendix).
clavicle is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
humerus is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
radius is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
ulna is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
femur is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
tibia is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
fibula is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
metacarpal is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".
metatarsal is a long bone,
    as stated in LCD L33796, confer "A long bone is limited to a clavicle, humerus, radius, ulna, femur, tibia, fibula, metacarpal, or metatarsal".

section applicability is:

% The article's certificate of medical necessity (dates of service before
% 2023) and modifiers are not modelled: none of the policy's own.
osteogenesis_stimulators has no specific documentation requirements.

% The codes this policy decides: the three noninvasive stimulators, the
% coupling gel, and the invasive stimulator the DME MAC does not process.
rule osteo_codes with provenance Policy Article A52513,
        confer "Osteogenesis stimulators are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is osteogenesis_stimulators
    if the code is in ["E0747", "E0748", "E0760", "A4559", "E0749"].

% Their benefit: durable medical equipment, except the invasive stimulator.
rule osteo_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52513,
        confer "Osteogenesis stimulators are covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the code is in ["E0747", "E0748", "E0760", "A4559"].

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The non-spinal electrical stimulator (E0747): any of three criteria.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule osteo_nonspinal with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "A non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator (E0747) is covered only if any of the following criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0747"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator.

% Nonunion of a long bone fracture, documented by the two sets of
% radiographs.
rule osteo_nonspinal_nonunion with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Nonunion of a long bone fracture (see Appendices section) defined as radiographic evidence that fracture healing has ceased for three or more months prior to starting treatment with the osteogenesis stimulator":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator
    if the beneficiary has a fracture of a bone
    and the bone is a long bone
    and the nonunion of the fracture of the beneficiary is documented by radiographs before treatment.

% The two sets of radiographs: before treatment, at least 90 days apart,
% each with multiple views, and the written interpretation (the finding).
rule osteo_radiographs with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Nonunion of a long bone fracture must be documented by a minimum of two sets of radiographs obtained prior to starting treatment with the osteogenesis stimulator, separated by a minimum of 90 days, each including multiple views of the fracture site, and with a written interpretation by a treating practitioner stating that there has been no clinically significant evidence of fracture healing between the two sets of radiographs":
the nonunion of the fracture of a beneficiary is documented by radiographs before treatment
    if the radiographs of the fracture of the beneficiary obtained on a date include multiple views of the fracture site
    and the radiographs of the fracture of the beneficiary obtained on an other date include multiple views of the fracture site
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 90
    and osteogenesis stimulator treatment of the beneficiary started on a third date
    and the third date is an other number days after the other date
    and the other number >= 0
    and the finding fracture healing ceased about the beneficiary is established.

% Failed fusion of a joint other than in the spine, nine months (274 days)
% after the last surgery.
rule osteo_nonspinal_failed_fusion with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Failed fusion of a joint other than in the spine where a minimum of nine months has elapsed since the last surgery":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator
    if the beneficiary has a failed fusion of a joint
    and it is not the case that
        the joint is spine
    and the last fusion surgery of the beneficiary was on a date
    and osteogenesis stimulator treatment of the beneficiary started on an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 274.

% Congenital pseudarthrosis.
rule osteo_nonspinal_pseudarthrosis with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Congenital pseudarthrosis":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a non-spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents congenital pseudarthrosis.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The spinal electrical stimulator (E0748): any of three criteria.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule osteo_spinal with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "A spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator (E0748) is covered only if any of the following criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "E0748"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for a spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator.

% Failed spinal fusion, nine months (274 days) after the last surgery.
rule osteo_spinal_failed_fusion with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Failed spinal fusion where a minimum of nine months has elapsed since the last surgery":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator
    if the beneficiary has a failed fusion of spine
    and the last fusion surgery of the beneficiary was on a date
    and osteogenesis stimulator treatment of the beneficiary started on an other date
    and the other date is a number days after the date
    and the number >= 274.

% Following a multilevel spinal fusion: three or more vertebrae.
rule osteo_spinal_multilevel with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "A multilevel spinal fusion is one which involves 3 or more vertebrae (e.g., L3-L5, L4-S1, etc)":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator
    if the beneficiary had spinal fusion surgery on a date involving a number vertebrae
    and the number >= 3
    and osteogenesis stimulator treatment of the beneficiary started on an other date
    and the other date is after or equal to the date.

% Following a spinal fusion with a history of a previously failed fusion at
% the same site.
rule osteo_spinal_previously_failed with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Following spinal fusion surgery where there is a history of a previously failed spinal fusion at the same site":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for a spinal electrical osteogenesis stimulator
    if the beneficiary had spinal fusion surgery on a date involving a number vertebrae
    and the beneficiary has a history of a previously failed spinal fusion at the same site
    and osteogenesis stimulator treatment of the beneficiary started on an other date
    and the other date is after or equal to the date.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The ultrasonic stimulator (E0760): all of the criteria; and the gel.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule osteo_ultrasonic with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "An ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator (E0760) is covered only if all of the following criteria are met":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is a covered ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator.

rule osteo_ultrasonic_covered with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "An ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator will be denied as not medically necessary if it is used with other noninvasive osteogenesis stimulators":
an item is a covered ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator
    if the HCPCS code of the item is "E0760"
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary meets the criteria for an ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator
    and it is not the case that
        the item is used concurrently with other noninvasive osteogenesis stimulators.

rule osteo_ultrasonic_criteria with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Nonunion of a fracture documented by a minimum of two sets of radiographs obtained prior to starting treatment with the osteogenesis stimulator, separated by a minimum of 90 days":
a beneficiary meets the criteria for an ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator
    if the beneficiary has a fracture of a bone
    and it is not the case that
        the bone is in [skull, vertebrae]
    and the nonunion of the fracture of the beneficiary is documented by radiographs before treatment
    and it is not the case that
        the fracture of the beneficiary is tumor related.

rule osteo_gel with provenance LCD L33796,
        confer "Ultrasound conductive coupling gel is covered and separately payable if an ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator is covered":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the HCPCS code of the item is "A4559"
    and the item is an accessory of a device
    and the device is a covered ultrasonic osteogenesis stimulator.
